<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Skylark.entitlements — the hardened runtime exceptions Skylark needs to keep
  working once it is signed for distribution.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL. Notarization requires the hardened runtime
  (`codesign --options runtime`), and the hardened runtime revokes capabilities
  that an unsigned local build simply has. Each one has to be asked for
  explicitly here. Get this wrong and the failure is nasty: the app notarizes
  successfully, installs cleanly, and then silently cannot hear you — which
  looks like a dictation bug rather than a signing one.

  Only add an entitlement with a reason written next to it. Every line here
  widens what the process may do, and the notary service reviews the list.

  NOT sandboxed: Skylark is Developer ID / direct distribution, not Mac App
  Store. The App Sandbox would break Accessibility text injection into other
  apps, which is the core of the product. `com.apple.security.app-sandbox` must
  stay absent.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Microphone. The whole product. Under the hardened runtime, audio input is
      denied without this even when the user has granted the TCC prompt, and
      `NSMicrophoneUsageDescription` in Info.plist is NOT a substitute — that
      string only controls what the prompt says.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>

    <!--
      Apple Events to other applications. `MediaPauseController` drives Music
      and Spotify over NSAppleScript to pause them while you dictate and resume
      afterwards (see NSAppleEventsUsageDescription in Info.plist). Without
      this the scripts fail with errAEEventNotPermitted (-1743) and playback
      keeps running over your dictation.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
